- sys/types
- sys/shrine

' Demand constructors are persistent values too. Select this contract artifact
' explicitly independently of the existing view constructors; publication never guesses type
' equivalence. The interpreter owns reads; published constructors own policy.
+  view_select
  ' The part of a read a computation observes. Missing slots are observations
  ' too: adding a previously absent slot must invalidate a cached answer.
  & view_select/all view_select/slots view_select/names
  + all
    :
  + slots
    : keys=row[path]
  + names
    :
+  view_read
  : source=safe select=view_select
+  view_plan
  ' What a woven ctor returns: a pure computation that pauses when it
  ' needs a named input.  A graft hands the branch to a name; nothing
  ' is copied.
  & view_plan/done view_plan/need view_plan/graft view_plan/fail
  + done
    : tree=axal[myth]
  + need
    : read=view_read next={\ res[axal[myth]]}view_plan
  + graft
    : source=safe
  + fail
    : reason=str
+  woven
  ' The woven ctor: get receives the cell's own slots, the care asked
  ' for, the path beneath the cell, and what to select, and returns a
  ' plan: done with a tree; need a read, which the kernel supplies
  ' before continuing; graft onto a name, nothing copied; or fail.
  ' It reads only what it asks for, and what it read is kept beside
  ' the answer, so a cached answer can be checked without rerunning.
  : get={\ myth care path view_select}view_plan
